---
title: Draw.io Compatible SVG Generation Instructions
description: Complete instructions for generating Draw.io compatible SVG diagrams
---

## Overview
Generate SVG diagrams that are fully compatible with draw.io/diagrams.net and can be edited using the VS Code Draw.io Integration extension. These files render as SVG images in markdown while remaining fully editable in the draw.io interface.

{% aside type="danger" title="CRITICAL: Do not use image tools" %}
Do not use image tools.  These diagrams are svgs not images.  They are just made up of code and you can generate and correct code.
{% /aside %}

## ⚠️ MANDATORY GENERATION PROCESS

**THE TWO MOST COMMON ERRORS:**
1. **Missing or incomplete mxCell data**
2. **Single-encoded ampersands instead of double-encoded** (see encoding section below)

Follow this exact process to avoid "Not a diagram file" errors:

1. **Plan Shape IDs**: Assign unique IDs to every rectangle, circle, line, and text group
2. **Create mxCell for Each Shape**: Every visual element needs corresponding Draw.io metadata
3. **HTML-Encode mxGraphModel**: Convert the complete XML structure to HTML entities
4. **DOUBLE-ENCODE AMPERSANDS**: Use `&amp;amp;` not `&amp;` in mxCell values within content attribute
5. **Match Coordinates Exactly**: SVG geometry must match mxCell geometry precisely  
6. **Test in Extension**: Verify the file opens for editing in VS Code Draw.io extension

**FAILURE TO INCLUDE COMPLETE mxCELL DATA = "NOT A DIAGRAM FILE" ERROR**
**FAILURE TO DOUBLE-ENCODE AMPERSANDS = "NOT A DIAGRAM FILE" ERROR**

## CRITICAL: Draw.io Editability Requirements

**ESSENTIAL FOR EDITABILITY**: The VS Code Draw.io extension requires complete mxCell data for every visual element. Simply having SVG shapes is NOT enough - each shape must have corresponding Draw.io metadata.

### Complete mxGraphModel Structure Required
The `content` attribute must contain a full mxGraphModel with mxCell entries for EVERY visual element:

```xml
content="&lt;mxGraphModel dx=&quot;1422&quot; dy=&quot;794&quot; grid=&quot;1&quot; gridSize=&quot;10&quot; guides=&quot;1&quot; tooltips=&quot;1&quot; connect=&quot;1&quot; arrows=&quot;1&quot; fold=&quot;1&quot; page=&quot;1&quot; pageScale=&quot;1&quot; pageWidth=&quot;827&quot; pageHeight=&quot;1169&quot;&gt;&lt;root&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;1&quot; parent=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;shape1&quot; value=&quot;Process Step&quot; style=&quot;rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; vertex=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry x=&quot;20&quot; y=&quot;20&quot; width=&quot;120&quot; height=&quot;60&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;connector1&quot; value=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;endArrow=classic;html=1;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; source=&quot;shape1&quot; target=&quot;shape2&quot; edge=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry width=&quot;50&quot; height=&quot;50&quot; relative=&quot;1&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;&gt;&lt;mxPoint x=&quot;140&quot; y=&quot;50&quot; as=&quot;sourcePoint&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxPoint x=&quot;180&quot; y=&quot;50&quot; as=&quot;targetPoint&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxGeometry&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;/root&gt;&lt;/mxGraphModel&gt;"
```

### Shape-to-mxCell Mapping Rules
**EVERY SVG element must have:**
1. **Unique ID**: `<rect id="shape1" ...>` matches `<mxCell id="shape1" ...>`
2. **Corresponding mxCell**: With exact geometry and styling
3. **Matching coordinates**: SVG and mxGeometry must be identical

### mxCell Requirements by Element Type

#### Rectangles/Shapes
```xml
<!-- SVG Element -->
<rect id="shape1" x="20" y="20" width="120" height="60" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000"/>

<!-- Corresponding mxCell (in content attribute, HTML encoded) -->
<mxCell id="shape1" value="Label Text" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;" parent="1" vertex="1">
  <mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="120" height="60" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
```

#### Connectors/Lines
```xml
<!-- SVG Element -->
<line id="connector1" x1="140" y1="50" x2="180" y2="50" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>

<!-- Corresponding mxCell -->
<mxCell id="connector1" value="" style="endArrow=classic;html=1;" parent="1" source="shape1" target="shape2" edge="1">
  <mxGeometry width="50" height="50" relative="1" as="geometry">
    <mxPoint x="140" y="50" as="sourcePoint"/>
    <mxPoint x="180" y="50" as="targetPoint"/>
  </mxGeometry>
</mxCell>
```

#### Text Elements
Text should be included in the parent shape's `value` attribute, NOT as separate mxCells.

### HTML Encoding for Content Attribute
The mxGraphModel XML must be HTML-encoded in the content attribute:
- `<` becomes `&lt;`
- `>` becomes `&gt;`
- `"` becomes `&quot;`
- `&` becomes `&amp;`

{% aside type="danger" title="CRITICAL: Double-Encoding Ampersands" %}
**MOST COMMON ENCODING ERROR**: Ampersands in mxCell `value` attributes require DOUBLE encoding!

❌ **WRONG**: `value="Sessions &amp; Memory"` (single-encoded)
✅ **CORRECT**: `value="Sessions &amp;amp; Memory"` (double-encoded)

**Why?** The content attribute itself is HTML-encoded, so characters within it need double encoding:
1. First encode for XML: `&` → `&amp;`
2. Then encode for HTML attribute: `&amp;` → `&amp;amp;`

When the browser decodes the content attribute, `&amp;amp;` becomes `&amp;`, which is then valid XML.

**Common text with ampersands**:
- "Settings & Configuration" → `&amp;amp;`
- "Load & Process" → `&amp;amp;`  
- "Storage & Memory" → `&amp;amp;`
- "Encrypt & Sign" → `&amp;amp;`

**Failure to double-encode ampersands will cause "Not a diagram file" errors!**
{% /aside %}

### Generation Process Requirements
1. **Plan the diagram**: List all shapes, connectors, and their IDs
2. **Generate SVG**: Create visual elements with unique IDs
3. **Generate mxCells**: Create corresponding mxCell for each element
4. **Encode mxGraphModel**: HTML-encode the complete mxGraphModel
5. **Embed in content**: Place encoded data in content attribute

## Critical Requirements

### File Naming Convention
**ESSENTIAL**: Always use `.drawio.svg` extension, NOT just `.svg`
- ✅ `flowchart.drawio.svg`
- ✅ `architecture.drawio.svg` 
- ❌ `diagram.svg`

This naming convention is required for the VS Code extension to recognize and edit the files.

### SVG Root Element Structure
```xml
<svg host="65bd71144e" 
     xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" 
     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" 
     version="1.1" 
     width="[WIDTH]px" 
     height="[HEIGHT]px" 
     viewBox="-0.5 -0.5 [WIDTH] [HEIGHT]"
     content="&lt;mxGraphModel&gt;&lt;root&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;1&quot; parent=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;/root&gt;&lt;/mxGraphModel&gt;">
```

### Required Metadata Structure
```xml
<defs>
  <!-- Arrow markers and other definitions -->
</defs>
<g>
  <!-- All diagram content goes here -->
</g>
```

## CRITICAL: Draw.io Editability Requirements

**MANDATORY**: For the VS Code Draw.io extension to recognize and edit the file, you MUST include complete mxCell data for every visual element in the content attribute.

### Complete mxGraphModel Structure
The content attribute must contain an mxCell entry for EVERY shape, text, and line:

```xml
content="&lt;mxGraphModel dx=&quot;1422&quot; dy=&quot;794&quot; grid=&quot;1&quot; gridSize=&quot;10&quot;&gt;&lt;root&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;1&quot; parent=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;shape1&quot; value=&quot;Main Config&quot; style=&quot;rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dbeafe;strokeColor=#1e40af;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; vertex=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry x=&quot;250&quot; y=&quot;60&quot; width=&quot;300&quot; height=&quot;80&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;arrow1&quot; style=&quot;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; source=&quot;shape1&quot; target=&quot;shape2&quot; edge=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry relative=&quot;1&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;/root&gt;&lt;/mxGraphModel&gt;"
```

### Shape-to-Cell Mapping Rules
**Every SVG element MUST have:**
1. A unique `id` attribute
2. A corresponding `mxCell` in the content attribute  
3. Exact geometry coordinates that match

### mxCell Requirements by Element Type

#### Rectangles/Boxes
```xml
<!-- SVG Element -->
<rect id="config-box" x="250" y="60" width="300" height="80" rx="8" ry="8" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#1e40af"/>
<text x="400" y="100">astro.config.mjs</text>

<!-- Corresponding mxCell (HTML-encoded in content attribute) -->
<mxCell id="config-box" value="astro.config.mjs" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dbeafe;strokeColor=#1e40af;strokeWidth=2;" parent="1" vertex="1">
  <mxGeometry x="250" y="60" width="300" height="80" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
```

#### Lines/Arrows
```xml
<!-- SVG Element -->
<line id="arrow1" x1="400" y1="140" x2="400" y2="200" stroke="#1e40af" marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>

<!-- Corresponding mxCell -->
<mxCell id="arrow1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;html=1;strokeColor=#1e40af;" parent="1" source="config-box" target="integration1" edge="1">
  <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>
```

#### Text Elements
Include text in the parent shape's `value` attribute, not as separate mxCells.

### HTML Encoding for Content Attribute
The mxGraphModel XML must be HTML-encoded when placed in the content attribute:
- `<` becomes `&lt;`
- `>` becomes `&gt;`  
- `"` becomes `&quot;`
- `&` becomes `&amp;`

{% aside type="danger" title="CRITICAL: Double-Encoding Ampersands" %}
**MOST COMMON ENCODING ERROR**: Ampersands in mxCell `value` attributes require DOUBLE encoding!

❌ **WRONG**: `value="Sessions &amp; Memory"` (single-encoded)
✅ **CORRECT**: `value="Sessions &amp;amp; Memory"` (double-encoded)

**Why?** The content attribute itself is HTML-encoded, so characters within it need double encoding:
1. First encode for XML: `&` → `&amp;`
2. Then encode for HTML attribute: `&amp;` → `&amp;amp;`

When the browser decodes the content attribute, `&amp;amp;` becomes `&amp;`, which is then valid XML.

**Common text with ampersands**:
- "Settings & Configuration" → `&amp;amp;`
- "Load & Process" → `&amp;amp;`  
- "Storage & Memory" → `&amp;amp;`
- "Encrypt & Sign" → `&amp;amp;`

**Failure to double-encode ampersands will cause "Not a diagram file" errors!**
{% /aside %}

### Content Attribute Generation Process
1. Create the complete mxGraphModel XML with all mxCells
2. HTML-encode the entire XML string
3. Place in the content attribute of the SVG root

### Code Span Integration  
Link shapes to code references:
```xml
<rect id="shape1" data-code-ref="functionName" .../>
```

## Shape Guidelines

### Basic Shapes
- **Rectangles**: `<rect x="20" y="20" width="120" height="60" rx="5" ry="5">`
- **Circles**: `<circle cx="80" cy="80" r="40">` or `<ellipse cx="80" cy="50" rx="60" ry="30">`
- **Text**: Always use `<text>` with proper positioning and styling
- **Lines**: Use `<line>` or `<path>` with arrow markers

### Standard Styling
```xml
<!-- Rectangle with standard styling -->
<rect x="20" y="20" width="120" height="60" rx="5" ry="5" 
      fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1"/>

<!-- Text with standard formatting -->
<text x="80" y="50" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
      font-family="Helvetica" font-size="12" fill="#000000">Label Text</text>

<!-- Circle/ellipse -->
<ellipse cx="200" cy="50" rx="40" ry="30" 
         fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1"/>
```

### Arrow Markers
Include in `<defs>` section:
```xml
<defs>
  <marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" 
          refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto">
    <polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#000000"/>
  </marker>
  <marker id="startArrow" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" 
          refX="0" refY="3.5" orient="auto">
    <polygon points="10 0, 0 3.5, 10 7" fill="#000000"/>
  </marker>
</defs>
```

### Lines with Arrows
```xml
<line x1="140" y1="50" x2="180" y2="50" 
      stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1" 
      marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
```

## Positioning and Layout

### Grid System
- Use 10px grid alignment (Draw.io default)
- Snap all coordinates to multiples of 10
- Standard spacing: 20px minimum between elements
- Page margins: 20px from edges

### Standard Dimensions
- **Process boxes**: 120x60px
- **Decision diamonds**: 80x80px  
- **Start/end ovals**: 120x40px
- **Circles**: 60-80px diameter
- **Text spacing**: 10px padding inside shapes

### Color Palette (Theme Compatible)
```xml
<!-- Primary colors -->
fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000"  <!-- Default white/black -->
fill="#e1f5fe" stroke="#0277bd"  <!-- Light blue -->
fill="#f3e5f5" stroke="#7b1fa2"  <!-- Light purple -->
fill="#e8f5e8" stroke="#388e3c"  <!-- Light green -->
fill="#fff3e0" stroke="#f57c00"  <!-- Light orange -->
fill="#ffebee" stroke="#d32f2f"  <!-- Light red -->

<!-- Avoid pure black/white for theme compatibility -->
fill="#f9fafb" stroke="#1f2937"  <!-- Better contrast -->
```

## Common Diagram Types

### Flowchart Elements
```xml
<!-- Start/End (Rounded rectangle) -->
<rect x="20" y="20" width="120" height="40" rx="20" ry="20" 
      fill="#e8f5e8" stroke="#388e3c" stroke-width="1"/>
<text x="80" y="40" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
      font-family="Helvetica" font-size="11">Start</text>

<!-- Process (Rectangle) -->
<rect x="20" y="80" width="120" height="60" rx="5" ry="5" 
      fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1"/>
<text x="80" y="110" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
      font-family="Helvetica" font-size="11">Process Step</text>

<!-- Decision (Diamond) -->
<path d="M 80 160 L 120 180 L 80 200 L 40 180 Z" 
      fill="#fff3e0" stroke="#f57c00" stroke-width="1"/>
<text x="80" y="180" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
      font-family="Helvetica" font-size="10">Decision?</text>
```

### Network/Architecture Elements
```xml
<!-- Server/Component -->
<rect x="20" y="20" width="100" height="80" rx="5" ry="5" 
      fill="#e1f5fe" stroke="#0277bd" stroke-width="2"/>
<text x="70" y="50" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
      font-family="Helvetica" font-size="11" font-weight="bold">Server</text>
<text x="70" y="70" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
      font-family="Helvetica" font-size="9">Database</text>

<!-- Connection with label -->
<line x1="120" y1="60" x2="180" y2="60" 
      stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1" 
      marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
<text x="150" y="55" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
      font-family="Helvetica" font-size="9">HTTP</text>
```

## Complete Template Example with Full mxCell Data

```xml
<svg host="65bd71144e" 
     xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" 
     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" 
     version="1.1" 
     width="400px" 
     height="300px" 
     viewBox="-0.5 -0.5 400 300"
     content="&lt;mxGraphModel dx=&quot;1422&quot; dy=&quot;794&quot; grid=&quot;1&quot; gridSize=&quot;10&quot; guides=&quot;1&quot; tooltips=&quot;1&quot; connect=&quot;1&quot; arrows=&quot;1&quot; fold=&quot;1&quot; page=&quot;1&quot; pageScale=&quot;1&quot; pageWidth=&quot;827&quot; pageHeight=&quot;1169&quot;&gt;&lt;root&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;1&quot; parent=&quot;0&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;start&quot; value=&quot;Start&quot; style=&quot;rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#e8f5e8;strokeColor=#388e3c;rounded=1;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; vertex=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry x=&quot;20&quot; y=&quot;20&quot; width=&quot;120&quot; height=&quot;40&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;arrow1&quot; value=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;endArrow=classic;html=1;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; source=&quot;start&quot; target=&quot;process&quot; edge=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry width=&quot;50&quot; height=&quot;50&quot; relative=&quot;1&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;&gt;&lt;mxPoint x=&quot;80&quot; y=&quot;60&quot; as=&quot;sourcePoint&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxPoint x=&quot;80&quot; y=&quot;100&quot; as=&quot;targetPoint&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxGeometry&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;process&quot; value=&quot;Load &amp;amp; Process&quot; style=&quot;rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#000000;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; vertex=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry x=&quot;20&quot; y=&quot;100&quot; width=&quot;120&quot; height=&quot;60&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;arrow2&quot; value=&quot;&quot; style=&quot;endArrow=classic;html=1;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; source=&quot;process&quot; target=&quot;end&quot; edge=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry width=&quot;50&quot; height=&quot;50&quot; relative=&quot;1&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;&gt;&lt;mxPoint x=&quot;80&quot; y=&quot;160&quot; as=&quot;sourcePoint&quot;/&gt;&lt;mxPoint x=&quot;80&quot; y=&quot;200&quot; as=&quot;targetPoint&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxGeometry&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;mxCell id=&quot;end&quot; value=&quot;End&quot; style=&quot;rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#ffebee;strokeColor=#d32f2f;rounded=1;&quot; parent=&quot;1&quot; vertex=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;mxGeometry x=&quot;20&quot; y=&quot;200&quot; width=&quot;120&quot; height=&quot;40&quot; as=&quot;geometry&quot;/&gt;&lt;/mxCell&gt;&lt;/root&gt;&lt;/mxGraphModel&gt;">
  
  <defs>
    <marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="7" 
            refX="10" refY="3.5" orient="auto">
      <polygon points="0 0, 10 3.5, 0 7" fill="#000000"/>
    </marker>
  </defs>
  
  <g>
    <!-- Start node -->
    <rect id="start" x="20" y="20" width="120" height="40" rx="20" ry="20" 
          fill="#e8f5e8" stroke="#388e3c" stroke-width="1"/>
    <text x="80" y="40" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
          font-family="Helvetica" font-size="11">Start</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow 1 -->
    <line id="arrow1" x1="80" y1="60" x2="80" y2="90" 
          stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1" 
          marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
    
    <!-- Process (Note: ampersand in text requires &amp;amp; in mxCell value above) -->
    <rect id="process" x="20" y="100" width="120" height="60" rx="5" ry="5" 
          fill="#ffffff" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1"/>
    <text x="80" y="130" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
          font-family="Helvetica" font-size="11">Load &amp; Process</text>
    
    <!-- Arrow 2 -->
    <line id="arrow2" x1="80" y1="160" x2="80" y2="190" 
          stroke="#000000" stroke-width="1" 
          marker-end="url(#arrowhead)"/>
    
    <!-- End node -->
    <rect id="end" x="20" y="200" width="120" height="40" rx="20" ry="20" 
          fill="#ffebee" stroke="#d32f2f" stroke-width="1"/>
    <text x="80" y="220" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="middle" 
          font-family="Helvetica" font-size="11">End</text>
  </g>
</svg>
```

### Key Elements in This Template:
1. **Proper content attribute**: Contains complete mxGraphModel with all shapes
2. **ID consistency**: Each SVG element ID matches its mxCell ID
3. **Complete mxCell data**: Every shape has geometry, styling, and connections
4. **HTML encoding**: All XML in content attribute is properly encoded
5. **Double-encoded ampersands**: Note `value="Load &amp;amp; Process"` - ampersands need `&amp;amp;` not `&amp;`
6. **Connection data**: Arrows have source/target references

## Quality Checklist

### MANDATORY Draw.io Compatibility Checks
- [ ] **File named with `.drawio.svg` extension**
- [ ] **Content attribute contains complete mxGraphModel**
- [ ] **Every SVG shape has corresponding mxCell with same ID**
- [ ] **All mxCell geometry matches SVG coordinates exactly**
- [ ] **mxGraphModel is properly HTML-encoded**
- [ ] **All shapes have unique IDs**
- [ ] **Connectors have proper source/target references**

### Before Generation
- [ ] Plan all shape IDs and their mxCell data
- [ ] SVG has proper xmlns declarations
- [ ] All coordinates use 10px grid alignment
- [ ] Consistent stroke-width (usually 1px)
- [ ] Arrow markers defined in `<defs>`

### After Generation
- [ ] **CRITICAL: File opens successfully in VS Code Draw.io extension**
- [ ] **CRITICAL: All elements are editable in draw.io interface**
- [ ] Valid XML structure (no unclosed tags)
- [ ] All text is readable and properly positioned
- [ ] Colors provide good contrast
- [ ] SVG renders correctly in markdown preview
- [ ] File works when embedded in GitHub README
- [ ] All arrows point in correct directions
- [ ] Consistent styling throughout

### Testing Workflow (ESSENTIAL)
1. **Generate the .drawio.svg file**
2. **Open in VS Code with Draw.io extension**
3. **VERIFY: File opens in draw.io editor (not error dialog)**
4. **VERIFY: Click on shapes to confirm they're editable**
5. **Test: Make a small edit and save**
6. **Confirm: File still renders in markdown preview**
7. **Test: GitHub embedding if applicable**

**If step 3 fails with "Not a diagram file" error, the mxCell data is incomplete or malformed.**

## Usage Examples

### In Markdown Files
```markdown
![System Architecture](./diagrams/architecture.drawio.svg)
```

### In GitHub README
```markdown
## System Flow
![Flow Diagram](./docs/flow.drawio.svg)
```

### VS Code Integration
1. Create/generate the `.drawio.svg` file
2. Open in VS Code with Draw.io extension installed
3. Click on the file to open in draw.io editor
4. Edit visually using draw.io interface
5. Save changes (preserves both SVG and edit data)
6. File remains renderable in markdown

## Best Practices

### Design Principles
1. **Simplicity**: Keep diagrams clean and uncluttered
2. **Consistency**: Use uniform spacing, colors, and fonts
3. **Hierarchy**: Use size and color to show importance
4. **Readability**: Ensure text is large enough and well-contrasted
5. **Purpose**: Include only essential information

### Technical Guidelines
1. Always validate XML structure
2. Use semantic grouping with `<g>` elements when needed
3. Include meaningful IDs for complex diagrams
4. Test cross-platform compatibility
5. Keep file sizes reasonable (under 1MB)
6. Use relative positioning when possible

### Collaboration Features
- Files work with draw.io collaborative editing
- Version control friendly (text-based format)
- Can be edited offline in VS Code
- Compatible with draw.io web interface
- Supports draw.io themes and styling

## Troubleshooting

## Troubleshooting

### "Not a diagram file" Error (Most Common Issue)
This error means the mxCell data is missing or malformed:

**Root Causes:**
- ❌ Missing or incomplete `content` attribute
- ❌ mxGraphModel not properly HTML-encoded
- ❌ SVG shapes without corresponding mxCells
- ❌ Malformed mxCell XML structure

**Solutions:**
1. **Verify content attribute exists and is complete**
2. **Check HTML encoding**: `<` = `&lt;`, `>` = `&gt;`, `"` = `&quot;`
3. **Ensure every SVG element has matching mxCell**
4. **Validate mxGraphModel XML structure**

**Quick Test**: Decode the content attribute and verify it's valid XML:
```xml
<!-- This should decode to valid XML like: -->
<mxGraphModel>
  <root>
    <mxCell id="0"/>
    <mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>
    <mxCell id="shape1" value="Text" style="..." parent="1" vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="120" height="60" as="geometry"/>
    </mxCell>
  </root>
</mxGraphModel>
```

## Troubleshooting "Not a diagram file" Error

### Quick Diagnosis Checklist
When VS Code Draw.io extension shows "Not a diagram file":

1. **Check file extension**: Must be `.drawio.svg` (not `.svg`)
2. **Verify content attribute**: Must contain complete HTML-encoded mxGraphModel
3. **Count mxCells**: Should have one mxCell for every visual shape + 2 root cells
4. **Check HTML encoding**: Look for `&lt;` `&gt;` `&quot;` in content attribute
5. **Validate XML structure**: Ensure all mxCell tags are properly closed
6. **Match IDs**: Every SVG element ID should have corresponding mxCell ID

### Content Attribute Debugging
Extract and decode the content attribute to verify structure:
```
Expected: <mxGraphModel><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/><mxCell id="shape1"...
Found: <mxGraphModel><root><mxCell id="0"/><mxCell id="1" parent="0"/></root></mxGraphModel>
Problem: Missing shape mxCells
```

### Common Fixes
- **Missing mxCells**: Add mxCell entry for every shape
- **Wrong encoding**: HTML-encode the mxGraphModel XML
- **Ampersands not double-encoded**: Change `&amp;` to `&amp;amp;` in mxCell values within content attribute
- **ID mismatch**: Ensure SVG IDs match mxCell IDs exactly
- **Empty content**: Include complete mxGraphModel structure
- **Malformed XML**: Validate all opening/closing tags

### Testing Workflow
1. Generate the .drawio.svg file with complete mxCell data
2. Try opening in VS Code Draw.io extension  
3. If error occurs, check content attribute structure
4. Fix missing/incorrect mxCell entries
5. Re-test until file opens for editing

## Common Issues
- **File won't open in draw.io**: Check `.drawio.svg` extension and complete mxCell data
- **SVG doesn't render**: Validate XML structure and viewBox dimensions
- **Text positioning off**: Verify `text-anchor` and `dominant-baseline` attributes
- **Arrows not showing**: Ensure marker definitions in `<defs>` and proper `marker-end` references
- **Colors look wrong**: Test with both light/dark themes, avoid pure black/white
- **Shapes not editable**: Missing or incorrect mxCell data for specific elements
- **Connection errors**: Check `source` and `target` attributes in connector mxCells
- **"Not a diagram file" with ampersands**: Check if text like "Sessions & Memory" is encoded as `&amp;amp;` not `&amp;` in the content attribute

### Debug Steps for mxCell Issues
1. **Extract content attribute value**
2. **HTML-decode the mxGraphModel**
3. **Validate XML structure**
4. **Check each mxCell has required attributes**:
   - `id` (unique)
   - `parent` (usually "1")
   - `vertex="1"` for shapes OR `edge="1"` for connectors
   - `<mxGeometry>` with correct coordinates
5. **Verify ID consistency between SVG and mxCells**

### Validation Tools
- Use XML validator for structure
- Test in multiple markdown renderers
- Verify in VS Code draw.io extension
- Check GitHub rendering if applicable

This comprehensive guide ensures generated SVG files are fully compatible with draw.io while remaining perfectly renderable as standard SVG images in any markdown context.

## FINAL CHECKLIST FOR CODE ASSISTANTS

Before delivering any .drawio.svg file, verify:

### File Structure ✅
- [ ] Filename ends with `.drawio.svg`
- [ ] SVG root has `content` attribute with HTML-encoded mxGraphModel
- [ ] All SVG elements have unique `id` attributes
- [ ] Content attribute includes complete mxGraphModel with all required mxCells

### mxCell Requirements ✅  
- [ ] Root cells: `<mxCell id="0"/>` and `<mxCell id="1" parent="0"/>`
- [ ] Shape cells: One mxCell for every rectangle, circle, path element
- [ ] Connector cells: One mxCell for every line/arrow with source/target refs
- [ ] Geometry match: mxCell coordinates exactly match SVG coordinates
- [ ] Proper encoding: All `<` `>` `"` in content are HTML-encoded
- [ ] **CRITICAL**: Ampersands in mxCell values are DOUBLE-encoded as `&amp;amp;` not `&amp;`

### Testing ✅
- [ ] Content attribute contains more than just root cells
- [ ] mxCell count = number of visual shapes + 2 root cells + connectors  
- [ ] File would open successfully in VS Code Draw.io extension
- [ ] SVG renders correctly in markdown

**REMEMBER**: A file that only renders as SVG but can't be edited is NOT a proper .drawio.svg file.
